        "message": "LU-17000 lnet: print in6_addr with %pI6c, not %pIS\n\nksocknal_inet6addr_event() and kiblnd_inet6addr_event() log\n&ifa6->addr, a bare struct in6_addr, with %pIS.  That specifier expects\na struct sockaddr: the kernel reads sa_family out of the first two\nbytes of the address and then formats the rest as a sockaddr_in or\nsockaddr_in6.  Adding addresses to an interface on a node with a tcp NI\nshows what that produces:\n\n  address          %pISc (before)      %pI6c (after)\n  2001:db8::1      (einval)            2001:db8::1\n  fe80::dead:1     (einval)            fe80::dead:1\n  200::1           0.0.0.0             200::1\n  a00::1           ::1:4000:0:0:0      a00::1\n\nThe first two have leading bytes that name no address family.  200::1\nbegins 02 00, which reads back as AF_INET, so sin_addr is taken from\nbytes 4..7 of the address.  a00::1 begins 0a 00, which reads back as\nAF_INET6, and sin6_addr sits 8 bytes into a sockaddr_in6 - so the\nkernel formats bytes 8..23 of a 16-byte object.  The 4000 in that\noutput is inet6_ifaddr.prefix_len (64), read 8 bytes past the end of\nthe in6_addr, and %pISc goes on to read sin6_scope_id past that.\n\nUse %pI6c.  There is no sockaddr to hand to %pIS instead: an\ninet6addr notifier is passed a struct inet6_ifaddr, which carries an\nin6_addr with no family, no port and no scope.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: e5903f8b5319 (\"LU-17460 lnet: support IPv6 for link state\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I1986a668e71085ac62da6ef2a888aee4f43d215d\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68497\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
